DS.push([5,'Four people are discussing whether the town library should open on Sundays.',['Sunday is the only day many working families can visit.','Staff already work long hours and deserve a proper day off.','Opening hours should follow the needs of readers, not the convenience of employees.','A library that is closed when people are free is hardly a service at all.'],[['Which phrase in comment 4 most strongly suggests disapproval?','hardly a service at all',['when people are free','a library','is closed'],'Loaded Language'],['Which comment treats the staff’s wishes as less important than the readers’?','comment 3',null,'Assumptions'],['Which comment gives a reason based on the staff’s wellbeing?','comment 2',null,'Assumptions']]],[6,'Four students are debating whether school should start later in the morning.',['Teenagers are biologically wired to sleep later, so early starts leave them tired and slow.','If school starts later it will finish later, and sport and part-time jobs will be squeezed out.','Everyone manages to get up for the things they enjoy, so tiredness is really a question of attitude.','Several schools that moved their start times report fewer late arrivals.'],[['Which word in comment 1 most strongly suggests that the cause is beyond the students’ control?','wired',['teenagers','sleep','slow'],'Loaded Language'],['Which comment assumes that tiredness has only one cause?','comment 3',null,'Assumptions'],['Which comment predicts a downside of the change?','comment 2',null,'Assumptions']]],[7,'A council is debating whether to replace a statue of a founding mayor with a new work of public art.',['A statue is a statement about who a town chooses to honour, and that choice should be renewed over time.','Remove it and you erase the town’s history.','History lives in books and archives, not in lumps of bronze on street corners.','Whatever the council decides, the cost should not fall on ratepayers.'],[['Which word in comment 2 most strongly suggests that removal is harmful?','erase',['remove','town’s','history'],'Loaded Language'],['Which comment assumes that a statue is the only way to keep history alive?','comment 2',null,'Assumptions'],['Which comment disagrees with comment 2 by saying history is kept elsewhere?','comment 3',null,'Assumptions']]]);
RD.push([2,"The new girl sat at the back and said nothing. At lunch she opened a small tin and took out a single orange, peeling it in one long curl. Without a word she placed a segment on the bench beside each of us, then smiled for the first time.",[["What does the girl’s action show?","She wants to be friendly",["She is afraid of the others","She dislikes oranges","She is very hungry"],"Inference"],["How did she peel the orange?","In one long curl",["In small pieces","With a knife","Quickly in half"],"Literal Comprehension"],["How does the mood change by the end of the passage?","from awkward silence to warmth",["from joy to fear","from anger to sadness","from boredom to anger"],"Change in Feeling"]]],
[4,"By midsummer the lake had shrunk to a brown saucer, and the old jetty stood stranded on dry mud, its legs like the legs of a heron that had waited too long for rain. Children dared each other to walk out to its end. Nobody dared the other thing, which was to look down.",[["The jetty is compared to a heron to suggest that it","looks stranded and patient",["is graceful and fast","is made of feathers","is about to fly"],"Writer's Technique"],["Why might nobody dare to look down?","The exposed lake bed is frightening or unpleasant",["The jetty is very high","The children are afraid of heights","There are sharks below"],"Inference"],["“stranded” most nearly means","left helpless in an unsuitable place",["built very strongly","painted brightly","washed clean"],"Vocabulary in Context"]]],
[6,"The museum’s newest exhibit is a room of silence. Visitors surrender their phones, then sit on plain benches while nothing is played, shown or explained. Critics have called it a gimmick; yet on the day I visited, the queue was an hour long, and people emerged blinking, talkative and a little embarrassed, like swimmers who had stayed under too long.",[["The writer’s attitude to the exhibit is best described as","intrigued but measured",["scornful","uncritically enthusiastic","indifferent"],"Tone & Purpose"],["The comparison with swimmers suggests that visitors","needed a moment to readjust after an absorbing experience",["were unhappy with the exhibit","had learned to swim","were frightened of water"],"Writer's Technique"],["The writer mentions the hour-long queue to","suggest that the critics may be wrong",["complain about crowds","show that the exhibit is cheap","explain why phones are banned"],"Purpose of a Detail"]]],
[7,"Efficiency is a virtue we rarely examine. A system optimised for speed may be admirable until the moment something goes wrong, at which point the absence of slack, of spare capacity, of anyone with time to think, turns a small fault into a catastrophe. Resilience, the ability to absorb a shock, is often the price of a little waste.",[["According to the writer, a very efficient system is dangerous because","it has no spare capacity to cope with problems",["it always runs too slowly","it needs more workers","it wastes too many resources"],"Inference"],["“slack” as used in the passage most nearly means","spare capacity",["looseness of rope","laziness","speed"],"Vocabulary in Context"],["The final sentence is mainly intended to","suggest that some inefficiency has value",["praise wasteful systems","explain how shocks are absorbed","criticise slow workers"],"Purpose of a Detail"]]]);
Object.assign(G['Reading Comprehension'],{
'Punctuation':d=>{let[a,A]=pk(PC1),[b,B]=pk(PC2),n=pk(PN),v=pk(PVB),nm=A.replace(/’/g,'');return mc(`The sentence below has no punctuation. Choose the option with the correct punctuation.<br><b>${a} ${v} ${n.toLowerCase()} ${b}</b>`,`“${A},” ${v} ${n}, “${B}.”`,[`“${nm},” ${v} ${n}, “${B}.”`,`“${A}”, ${v} ${n} “${B}”.`,`${A}, ${v} ${n}, ${B}.`,`“${A},” ${v} ${n}. “${B}.”`])},
'Sentence Rewriting':d=>{let[c,a,ap,b]=pk(SRT),nn=pk(NM),f=s=>s.replace(/%/g,nn),O=sh(['so','unless','although','because','if'].filter(x=>x!=c));return mc(`Read this sentence.<br><i>${cap(c)} ${f(a)}, ${b}.</i><br>If the sentence is rewritten to begin <b>${cap(b)}</b>, what should the ending be?`,`${c} ${f(a)}.`,[`${O[0]} ${f(a)}.`,`${c} ${f(ap)}.`,`${O[1]} ${f(ap)}.`])},
'Spelling & Grammar':d=>{let[e1,e2]=sh(SPN).slice(0,2),t=pk(SPC),f=(a,b)=>t.replace('${a}',a).replace('${b}',b),sw=w=>w.slice(0,2)+w[3]+w[2]+w.slice(4);return mc(`Choose the option that corrects the spelling errors in this sentence.<br><i>${f(e1[0],e2[0])}</i>`,f(e1[1],e2[1]),[f(e1[1],e2[0]),f(e1[0],e2[1]),f(e1[0],e2[0].slice(0,-1)),f(e1[1],sw(e2[1])),f(sw(e1[1]),e2[1])])},
'Filling the Gap':d=>{let c=GAP.filter(x=>Math.abs(x[3]-d)<=2),x=pk(c.length?c:GAP);return mc(`Which word best fills the gap?<br><i>${x[0]}</i>`,x[1],x[2])}});
Object.assign(MIN,{'Reading Comprehension|Filling the Gap':2});
