QT.length=0;QT.push(['A candle loses nothing by lighting another.','generosity that diminishes the giver not at all',['prudence in conserving scarce resources','indifference to waste','envy of another’s success'],5],['A ship in harbour is safe, but that is not what ships are for.','the necessity of courting risk in order to fulfil one’s purpose',['the wisdom of avoiding every danger','the importance of maintaining equipment','the superiority of travel over rest'],6],['Anyone can begin; the test is who finishes.','perseverance as the true measure of commitment',['the advantage of a swift start','the role of fortune in success','the value of public approval'],5],['The map is not the territory.','a representation should never be mistaken for the reality it depicts',['explorers must draw accurate charts','distance is easier to measure than terrain','travel is preferable to study'],7],['A thorn teaches the hand what a book cannot.','knowledge acquired through direct experience',['the hazards of the garden','the inadequacy of all written knowledge','the value of caution in handling plants'],6],['Water the roots, not the leaves.','remedying underlying causes rather than superficial symptoms',['the economy of conserving water','the horticultural benefit of irrigation','the neglect of neatness'],6],['A small leak will sink a great ship.','the cumulative danger of neglected minor flaws',['the strength of large vessels','the unpredictability of the sea','the importance of speed in repair'],6],['We see things not as they are, but as we are.','perception is coloured by the observer’s own disposition',['eyesight deteriorates with age','honesty requires courage','judgement should be swift'],7],['Fall seven times, stand up eight.','indomitable resilience in the face of repeated failure',['the inevitability of clumsiness','the superiority of numerical precision','the virtue of avoiding risk'],5],['What is spoken may vanish; what is written must answer for itself.','the accountability that permanence imposes on the written word',['the superiority of oral tradition','the transience of all language','the importance of rapid communication'],7],['Patience is not the waiting; it is how you behave while you wait.','composure in conduct rather than mere endurance of delay',['the inevitability of delay','the advantage of hope','the necessity of obedience'],6],['The lamp does not argue with the dark; it simply shines.','influence exerted through example rather than dispute',['the futility of resisting adversity','the avoidance of all conflict','the fear of obscurity'],6]);
